     This is actually expected behavior after the previous
warning.  A dead monster was put on the map erroneously,
then after the next round of monster movement a dead monster
was found, without one having been killed during that turn.
Now it is finally gone.

> The "placing defunct monster onto map?" message appears to come from
> steed.c line 632, which makes me think it has something to do
> with my pet (a warhorse, which had shortly before gotten polymorphed
> into a centaur).

     The fact that this code is in steed.c has absolutely
no relation to whether or not your pet is involved.  However,
the fact that a dead monster was put on the map as you changed
levels suggests that it might have been an adjacent monster
which accompanied you during level change, which would usually
be a pet (where "usually" refers to the adjacent accompanier
part, not the dead monster sticking around part).  Or else
there was a dead monster on the level which didn't get removed
prior to saving bones.  Neither of those things should happen,
and any circumstance which might have led to either of them
must be unusual or lots of players would be encountering this.

